        "subtype": "bot_message",
        "text": "*[Bug 18260] method L-BFGS-B does not respect the bounds*\n<https:\/\/bugs.r-project.org\/show_bug.cgi?id=18260>\n\nPeter Dalgaard (<mailto:pd.mes@cbs.dk|pd.mes@cbs.dk>) changed:\n\n           What    |Removed                     |Added\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n             Status|TRIAGED                     |CONFIRMED\n                 CC|                            |pd.mes@cbs.dk\n\n--- Comment #6 from Peter Dalgaard (<mailto:pd.mes@cbs.dk|pd.mes@cbs.dk>) ---\nThanks to Michael C. for the analysis. I think it is correct in pinpointing\nthat the issue is that the Hessian computation needs to learn to work with only\npoints inside the constraining box. However, even with the correct computation,\nwe would still get the Hessian of the unconstrained problem, so we cannot claim\nthat this is \"as documented\" behaviour. Consequently, I'm moving this to\nCONFIRMED.",
        "username": "r-bugs notifier",
        "icons": {
            "emoji": ":robot_face:"
        },
        "type": "message",
        "ts": "1783605918.134249",
        "bot_id": "B06769YJX9Q",
        "app_id": "A024R9PQM",
        "blocks": [
            {
                "type": "rich_text",
                "block_id": "lGK",
                "elements": [
                    {
                        "type": "rich_text_section",
                        "elements": [
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "[Bug 18260] method L-BFGS-B does not respect the bounds",
                                "style": {
                                    "bold": true
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "\n"
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "link",
                                "url": "https:\/\/bugs.r-project.org\/show_bug.cgi?id=18260"
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "\n\nPeter Dalgaard ("
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "link",
                                "url": "mailto:pd.mes@cbs.dk",
                                "text": "pd.mes@cbs.dk"
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": ") changed:\n\n           What    |Removed                     |Added\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n             Status|TRIAGED                     |CONFIRMED\n                 CC|                            |pd.mes@cbs.dk\n\n--- Comment #6 from Peter Dalgaard ("
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "link",
                                "url": "mailto:pd.mes@cbs.dk",
                                "text": "pd.mes@cbs.dk"
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": ") ---\nThanks to Michael C. for the analysis. I think it is correct in pinpointing\nthat the issue is that the Hessian computation needs to learn to work with only\npoints inside the constraining box. However, even with the correct computation,\nwe would still get the Hessian of the unconstrained problem, so we cannot claim\nthat this is \"as documented\" behaviour. Consequently, I'm moving this to\nCONFIRMED."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ]
            }
        ]
